QMacStyle: Draw QProgressBar with QPainter under Liquid Glass

Backport of qtbase ae6f389942d60959fcae0f5d9f2bb6eadd8efb06 (Qt 6.10.0,
QTBUG-138947), which is not in 6.8.5.

With Liquid Glass an NSProgressIndicator draws nothing into the backing
store, so a QProgressBar stays empty. Upstream draws the groove and the
bar with QPainter instead (drawProgressBar()) when Qt runs with Liquid
Glass.

The backport differs from upstream:
- Only the Liquid Glass path is added, as a branch of its own at the top
  of CE_ProgressBarContents, and the code for the old look stays as it is
  in 6.8.5. Upstream also moved [ipi startAnimation] from the start of the
  style animation into the drawing of every frame, while stopAnimation is
  still sent once. The animator count of QIndeterminateProgressIndicator
  then never drops back to 0, and after the bar leaves the indeterminate
  state the hidden indicator stays in the window and keeps animating. The
  Liquid Glass branch does not use the indicator at all.
- drawProgressBar() counts the value from the minimum and keeps it in the
  range, as QCommonStyle does. Upstream (dev, October 2026) divides the
  value itself by the range, so a range that does not start at 0 is
  filled wrongly, and a reset QProgressBar (value minimum - 1) draws a
  sliver left of the groove.
- drawProgressBar() is defined after resolveCurrentNSView(): the code next
  to QMacStyle::create(), where upstream puts it, is different in 6.8.

Without Liquid Glass nothing changes: the old look renders byte for byte
as with 6.8.5.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/styles/mac/qmacstyle_mac.mm
@@ -2232,7 +2232,99 @@
 {
